course: dictionary
lesson: 3632
title: Fingernail in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fingernail is the hard, thin layer that covers and protects the top of the tip of each finger. You can find its meaning from the words around it. In «scraped out sideways with a fingernail or card», a fingernail is something you use to pull a sting out of skin, so it must be part of your hand.
explain: Phrases such as «cut your fingernails», «bite your fingernails» and «under your fingernails» give more clues. Cut and bite tell you that fingernails are part of your body, and under tells you that they can hold dirt. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Scrub under the hard layer on your fingertip" makes sense.
explain: Some phrases do not mean what their words say. «Hang on by your fingernails» does not mean a nail holding you up; it means only just manage. Read the whole phrase, not each word alone.
fact: A fingernail is the hard, thin layer on the top of the tip of each finger.
fact: Fingernails are made of keratin, the same material as hair and animal claws and horns.
fact: Fingernails keep growing, so we need to cut them.
fact: Dirt and germs can hide under fingernails, so scrub them when you wash your hands and keep them short.
fact: «Hang on by your fingernails» means only just manage.
exercise: What is a fingernail? | *The hard, thin layer that covers and protects the tip of each finger | A type of glove | A small bone inside your hand | A soft pad that you can feel on your palm
exercise: Why should you scrub under your fingernails when you wash your hands? | To stop them from being cut | Because they are sharp and need polishing | To make them grow faster and longer | *Because germs and dirt can hide there
exercise: What does the phrase «hang on by your fingernails» mean? | Climb a very tall tree | Hold on tightly with your hands | *Only just manage | Be very tidy and neat
test: What does «cut your fingernails» tell you about fingernails? | Fingernails can fly away from your hands | *Fingernails keep growing and need trimming | Fingernails stop growing at the age of five | Fingernails are made of glass and never grow
test: Why is biting your fingernails a bad habit? | *Biting spreads germs | It is a Scottish word | It makes them hard and shiny | It makes them grow longer
exam: In «frogs small enough to sit on your fingernail», which word is the clue that a fingernail is small? | *small | enough | frogs | sit
